# Live field snapshots are never committed.
#
# They are a point-in-time copy of what is in Kajabi, and they go stale the
# moment somebody edits a field. A stale snapshot in git is worse than none,
# because the next person reads it as canonical and diffs against the wrong
# thing. That is the exact failure this folder exists to prevent, and on
# 2026-08-17 459 KB of them were committed before the closing sweep caught it.
#
# The checker creates any file it needs, so nothing here has to exist in advance.
*.txt
